      "writtenOn": "2017-05-10T20:38:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a great catch.  Should I \n1) set min to 12.5 Hz, or\n2) change the driver such that in the case where it reads the FIFO and it\u0027s invalid (i.e. accel in suspend while in low-power state), put the accel into normal mode, read the fifo, and then put it back into low-powered mode?  What I would more likely do is to check first to see if accel is in low-power mode, and if so, transition it to normal mode, then read FIFO, then transition it back to low-power mode.",
      "parentUuid": "faf6e8ea_32686245",
      "revId": "890986cfafaa437c4374ca36e69c6604ea965d27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
